<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Width" Type="Param">
<Data><T>Double</T><D>0.366003125</D></Data></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr" /></Item>
<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Crest Factor Reduction for 3GPP LTE DL Source&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;This example illustrates the usage of crest factor reduction for 3GPP LTE Downlink OFDMA signal using Keysight&amp;nbsp;SystemVue.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; The blocks used in this example are all from the standard &quot;Algorithm&quot; library within SystemVue. Where a standard algorithmic model was not sufficient, SystemVue&apos;s MATLAB Script model interface was used. To see the underlying MATLAB Script algorithm for these blcoks simply double click on the part symbol to see the source code.&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;Crest factor reduction (CFR) is a technique for reducing the peak-to average ratio (PAR) of an orthogonal frequency division multiplexing (OFDM) waveform. The algoithm used is based on a modified version of the algorithm in &quot;Constrained Clipping for Crest Factor Reduction in Multiple-user OFDM&quot;, In Proc. IEEE Radio and Wireless Symposium, pp.341-344, Jan. 2007.&amp;nbsp; This CFR algorithm consists of one IFFT, time domain polar clipping, in-band and out-of-band&amp;nbsp;post-processing and one FFT.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;In this workspace, 3GPP LTE downlink OFDMA signal just works on 10MHz bandwidth and the oversampling ratio is 4. It does not support other bandwidths (such as 1.4, 3, 5, 15 and 20 MHz).&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;LTE_DL_TxSpectrum just measures CCDF and spectrum without CFR.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;LTE_DL_Clipping has time domain clipping and measures&amp;nbsp; CCDF and spectrum. &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;LTE_DL_CFR_EVM implements CFR algorithm and measure&amp;nbsp;CCDF, spectrum and EVM.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;To save and display the spectrum data, please re-run these 3 designs and set the Data Persistence active in their Analysis.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;LTE_DL_CFR_BER measures BER/FER with CFR algorithm.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;In sub-network LTE_DL_Src_CFR, there are two MATLAB Script blocks (M1 and M2). M1 is for time domain clipping, its parameter threshold is the maximum permssible amplitude. M2 is for in-band and out-of-band post-processing, its parameter EVM_Th is the EVM threshold. Customers can modify both threshold of M1 and EVM_Th of M2.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;To save and display the spectrum data, please re-run &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="NotesDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;Rt14;Wm14</D></DVport>
